hello I am David Kaplan and I am NOT an  expert but I hope in this series to  learn as much as possible and explain it  to you the best way I can how did life  begin or at least how did life begin on  earth this is a question that many of us  are curious about and biologists are  working extremely hard to try to figure  it out one possible way this could have  happened is that there was a single or  single type of biological molecule that  eventually evolved into all of life now  a reason to think something like that  might have happened is that all life we  know on earth contains the same  biological molecules namely DNA RNA and  amino acids RNA is particularly  interesting because not only does it  encode genetic information  it also can act as a catalyst for  chemical reactions so one hope is that  RNA formed in the early times on the  earth before there was life and then  began to replicate itself so that sounds  may be very simple but it's  extraordinarily complicated first simply  by the fact that we don't know what the  early earth looked like however there  has been some progress in creating  subunits of RNA in a laboratory with  very simple chemical compounds an  ultraviolet light a subunit of RNA is a  phosphate molecule of sugar molecule and  a base there are four kinds of bases we  can label them with letters a GU and C  and those letters in a sense when you  have a strand of them tell a story they  contain an enormous amount of  information and there is your genetic  code  so if in a lab you can see how just from  chemical processes you can produce a  subunit of RNA and then watch RNA grow  and eventually if it's possible have it  replicated itself then you've at least  demonstrated the possibility of how life  could have formed now of course life  could have started not with RNA but  something even before that with  molecules that don't exist now it's a  proto RNA or perhaps life actually came  from another planet it landed here on a  meteor and it began to grow once it  found the favorable conditions of the  earth we don't know but our best way of  figuring it out is going through the  processes of reproducing what may have  happened at the beginning of life
 

